  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>Equation of ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>And equation of parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p>Now intersection point of ellipse and parabola will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now plotting the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/e7ac496b-07c5-4b63-96d0-c586ebc3c5ce.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 229px;\" /></p><p>Now randomly chosen points will be between origin and the intersecting point,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/fe39bf9a-2da7-44d0-8ecf-2e43c948cfff.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 267px;\" /></p><p>So, the integer points inside region are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Total number of ways to select three points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>12</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>220</mn></math></p><p>Required number of triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>7</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>73</mn></math></p><p>{Note: Points are taken such a way that distance between two points are multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;for example if we take points on line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;we can take following points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>so there will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;pairs from line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and will chose another point from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;line&nbsp;so triangle will have a positive area. Also note that height of the triangle will always be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>}</p><p>Hence, probability will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>73</mn><mn>220</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>",
